            "review_title": "Review at Hoang Yen Vietnamese Cuisine",
            "review_text": "Eli O\nAllentown, New Jersey91 contributions\n0\nFood is Good but the Service is AWFUL\nDec 2016 • Friends\nThe food was good, however the general impression due to the awful service is very unpleasant. Waiters seems to be absolutely not motivated to provide at least decent level of service.\n1. I asked the waitress to type the WiFi password in my phone. She did however the connection did not happen (apparently she made a typo). The waiter said \"OK\" and left me puzzled :(\n2. I ordered Thai tea asking to put small amount of ice. It took 5 times to explain (2 in English by me and 3 in Vietnamese by our local friend) what I wanted. The waiter brought the tea in the glass full of ice. When I pointed it out, the waiter took the glass, went somewhere, removed a couple of ice cubes from the top and returned the order to me.\n3. We asked to bring paper napkins. They did however they charged for the napkins!!! Our question \"Why\" was left unanswered (charge was $0.40 in a bill of ~$50), It was the first time I was in the restaurant where customers are charged for napkins.\n4. Cashew nuts present on the tables (before orders, as complimentary items as they seemed) were also subject to charge. \n\nAll attempts to ask waiters about anything were practically ignored or answered with no visible desire at least to understand what we (customers) are looking for. Any complains or questions were answered with \"No\", \"we cannot\", \"we pass it to the manager\", etc. \nNow it is up to you whether to go there or go to the restaurants next door.\nRead more\nValue\nService\nFood\nReview collected in partnership with this restaurant \nWritten December 29, 2016",
